# Naming: `juskel` (always lowercase)

In this repository, **`juskel` is always all lowercase** in code, folders, filenames, solution names, and log namespace filters.

## Required

| Item | Correct | Wrong |
|------|---------|-------|
| Solution | `juskel.sln` / `juskel.slnx` | `JusKel.sln` |
| Host project | `juskel.Api` | `JusKel.Api` |
| Shared project | `juskel.Shared` | `JusKel.Shared` |
| Module projects | `identity.Core`, `funding.Contracts` | — |
| Folders | `src/Host/juskel.Api/` | `src/Host/JusKel.Api/` |
| Log filter | `"juskel"` | `"JusKel"` |
| Dockerfile ENTRYPOINT | `juskel.Api.dll` | `JusKel.Api.dll` |

## C# conventions (unchanged)

- **Namespaces** follow folder names: `juskel.Api`, `identity.Core`
- **Types** remain PascalCase: `GlobalExceptionHandler`, `CreateOrderCommand`
- **Module names** remain PascalCase in project suffix: `identity.Contracts`, `funding.Core`

## User-facing docs

Marketing/legal prose (e.g. "JusKel UK" in footers) may use brand casing. **All technical artifacts** (code, paths, configs, cursor rules) use `juskel` lowercase.

## Agent duty

Before suggesting any path, project name, or namespace, verify it uses `juskel` not `JusKel`. Flag and correct any mixed-case `juskel` references.
